ITEMS = ((('what should i do right after getting sunburn', 'how do i treat sunburn quickly', 'what is the first step for painful sunburn', 'how to care for sunburn after a day outside', 'what helps sunburn on the shoulders', 'how do you handle bad sunburn', 'what to do when skin feels hot with sunburn', 'how can i ease sunburn at home', 'what is the best response to sunburn', 'how do i treat sunburn on holiday'), 'Get out of the sun straight away and cool the skin with a shower or damp cloth. Drink plenty of water and rest somewhere shaded. Ask a pharmacist about soothing lotion, and seek medical help if the sunburn is severe or the person feels unwell.'), (('should i use a cool compress on sunburn', 'how long to apply a cold compress to sunburn', 'does a cool bath help sunburn', 'can i put a damp towel on sunburn', 'how do i cool down sunburnt skin', 'is a cold flannel good for sunburn', 'why does cooling help painful sunburn', 'should i shower after sunburn', 'how often can i cool sunburn', 'what is the best way to cool sunburn'), 'A cool compress or shower can take the heat out of sunburn and ease discomfort. Use lukewarm water rather than ice, and pat the skin dry gently. Get medical advice if cooling does not help or the skin starts to blister widely.'), (('what lotion should i put on sunburn', 'is aloe vera good for sunburn', 'should i moisturise sunburnt skin', 'can i use aftersun on sunburn', 'what cream helps peeling sunburn', 'does calamine help sunburn', 'is it good to rub lotion into sunburn', 'what can i apply to sunburnt skin', 'should i use a healing cream for sunburn', 'how to moisturise skin after sunburn'), 'A simple moisturiser or aftersun lotion can help sunburnt skin feel less tight, and a pharmacist can suggest a soothing product. Apply it gently rather than rubbing. Ask a doctor if the skin is broken, weeping or unusually painful.'), (('should i pop blisters caused by sunburn', 'what to do with sunburn blisters', 'how do i treat blistered sunburn', 'is it ok to burst a sunburn blister', 'how to protect sunburn blisters', 'what if a sunburn blister breaks', 'should sunburn blisters stay covered', 'why not break blisters from sunburn', 'how to dress sunburn on the back', 'what helps painful blistered sunburn'), 'Leave sunburn blisters intact and cover them loosely with a clean soft cloth to stop clothing rubbing. Bursting them raises the risk of infection. Ask a pharmacist or doctor if many blisters form, the skin weeps or you develop a fever.'), (('what pain relief can i take for sunburn', 'should i take painkillers for sunburn', 'how to manage sunburn pain', 'can a pharmacist help with sunburn pain', 'is sunburn pain normal at night', 'what helps the pain of severe sunburn', 'can i use pain relief cream on sunburn', 'how do i sleep with painful sunburn', 'does sunburn hurt more when hot', 'when to get help for sunburn pain'), 'Speak to a pharmacist about suitable pain relief for sunburn and follow the instructions on the packet. Keep the skin cool and avoid taking more than the label allows. Get medical help if pain is severe, spreads or comes with dizziness.'), (('how do i treat sunburn on my face', 'what to do for sunburn around the eyes', 'can sunburn affect the lips', 'how to care for sunburn on the nose', 'should i cover sunburn on my face', 'what if sunburn reaches the eyelids', 'how do you soothe sunburnt cheeks', 'is sunburn on the face serious', 'what to do for sunburned ears', 'when to seek help for facial sunburn'), 'Keep facial sunburn cool and use a gentle moisturiser, avoiding the eyes unless a pharmacist recommends a product. Wear a soft hat and stay indoors while it settles. Seek medical advice if the eyelids swell, vision changes or the skin blisters badly.'), (('how do i treat sunburn in a child', 'what to do for sunburn on a baby', 'is sunburn worse for children', 'how to cool sunburn in kids', 'should i take a sunburnt child to the doctor', 'what helps sunburn in toddlers', 'how to protect a child with sunburn', 'can children get sunburn through cloud', 'what if a child has sunburn and fever', 'when to call for help with child sunburn'), 'Bring a sunburnt child indoors, cool the skin gently and offer water often. Use clothing and shade rather than more lotion while the skin is hot. Call a doctor if the child is very young, has blisters, seems drowsy or has a fever.'), (('what should i avoid doing with sunburn', 'can i go back in the sun with sunburn', 'should i rub sunburnt skin', 'is it bad to use soap on sunburn', 'should i apply ice to sunburn', 'can i wear tight clothes over sunburn', 'is popping sunburn skin a bad idea', 'what not to do when sunburnt at home', 'should i exfoliate after sunburn', 'can swimming make sunburn worse'), 'Avoid further sun exposure, scrubbing, ice and tight clothing while sunburn heals. Let peeling skin fall away on its own instead of picking it. Ask a pharmacist or doctor if the area becomes hot, swollen or smelly.'), (('when should i get help for bad sunburn', 'what are the signs of sunstroke from sunburn', 'can sunburn cause fever and chills', 'should i go to hospital for sunburn', 'what if sunburn makes me dizzy', 'when is sunburn an emergency', 'how do i know if sunburn is severe', 'what if sunburn covers most of my back', 'should i call a doctor for sunburn blisters', 'what symptoms with sunburn need urgent help'), 'Get urgent medical help if sunburn comes with confusion, dizziness, vomiting, a high fever or chills. Large areas of blistering also need assessment. Call emergency services if the person is lethargic, has a stiff neck or cannot keep fluids down.'), (('how can i stop sunburn happening again', 'what is the best sun protection after sunburn', 'should i use a higher factor sunscreen after sunburn', 'how often should i reapply sunscreen after sunburn', 'does clothing prevent sunburn', 'when is sunburn most likely', 'can i build a tolerance to sunburn', 'how to protect skin while sunburn heals', 'what clothes help avoid sunburn', 'is shade enough to prevent sunburn'), 'While sunburn heals, cover the skin with loose clothing and stay in the shade, especially around the middle of the day. Use a broad-spectrum sunscreen on exposed skin and reapply it as the label says. Ask a pharmacist for advice if your skin burns easily.'))
